Subject: [PATCH] TDP: query live properties and relay invalidations without GetAll caches

Apply this delta after the original acknowledgement/error-propagation revision.
The combined tdp-error-propagation.patch instead applies directly to v26.4.1;
do not apply both files to the same tree.

zbus 5.16.0 retains a failed initial GetAll as CachingResult::Cached{Err(e)}
forever and stops its cache update task. Set bypasses that cache, allowing a
successful write followed by a permanent old read error. Disable caching only
for the TDP backend proxy so each getter performs a live Properties.Get.

The generated value-based TDP notification relay has its own cached proxy.
Disabling caching on a PropertyStream would suppress all events, so use a
separate uncached PropertiesProxy receiving raw PropertiesChanged signals.
Forward only TdpLimit invalidations, without fetching a possibly failing value.
Annotate the session property as invalidates, which also disables the generic
cached value relay for this one property. Replace/abort the TDP signal task on
remote replacement/removal and abort it when the TDP service drops. Keep setter
notification asynchronous to preserve interface-lock/channel ordering.

Tests cover initial backend read/range failure, accepted Set15, recovery without
recreating the service/backend, and a healthy cached client receiving an
invalidation while the hardware getter fails then recovering to20. Hardware,
range and channel errors remain errors; no requested value is returned as state.
An external zbus client first initialized during an error can still poison its
own cache; this patch does not modify unrelated clients or the zbus library.

